p.src:
A schematic charge-conserving list of nucleon–pion field products is $\mathcal L_{N\pi}
\sim
\left\{
\Psi_p^\dagger\Psi_n\,\pi^+,\;
\Psi_n^\dagger\Psi_p\,\pi^-,\;
\Psi_p^\dagger\Psi_p\,\pi^0,\;
\Psi_n^\dagger\Psi_n\,\pi^0
\right\}.$ Only the field content and charge assignments are being displayed; relative coefficients, signs, and the spinor-matrix structure are not fixed here. The charge on the first pion field is fixed by testing a concrete reading: a neutron together with a positive pion may produce a proton, whereas using a negative pion there would turn negative incoming charge into positive outgoing charge. The conjugate term gives the opposite charged process.

